Subject: lha: also ask lhasa for the lower-case names (Quake's CD resource.1)

Walnut: the Quake 1.06 CD's resource.1 (resource.1?106_cd, matched by its checksum) gave
neither id1/pak0.pak nor id1/pak1.pak: "should have provided id1/pak0.pak?106 but did not",
so quake-registered could not be made from the CD at all. gdp asks lha for the names as its
data spells them (ID1/PAK0.PAK, ID1/PAK1.PAK); lhasa, Debian's lha, lists the names of an
MS-DOS archive in lower case (id1/pak0.pak) and extracts only exact matches, so it extracted
nothing and exited 0. Each name is now asked for as it is and in lower case; a name the
archive doesn't have is passed over. Tested in the games builder with the CD's resource.1:
quake-registered is built with both paks (checksums as gdp's data).

Forwarded: not yet (candidate for Debian)

diff --git a/game_data_packager/build.py b/game_data_packager/build.py
--- a/game_data_packager/build.py
+++ b/game_data_packager/build.py
@@ -1354,8 +1354,13 @@ class PackagingTask:
                         )
                         os.symlink(src, newsrc)
                         src = newsrc
+                    # lhasa (Debian's lha) lower-cases the names in an MS-DOS
+                    # archive and matches the names it is asked for exactly:
+                    # ask for each name as it is and in lower case
+                    names = list(dict.fromkeys(
+                        to_unpack + [n.lower() for n in to_unpack]))
                     check_call(
-                        ['lha', arg, src] + to_unpack,
+                        ['lha', arg, src] + names,
                         cwd=tmpdir,
                     )
                     self.consider_file_or_dir(tmpdir, provider=provider)
